From df4f25de985674f416e2dea68b1c36457eb1bd01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reed Law <reedlaw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:11:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add J7 diagnostic UART for Tang Primer 25K bring-up

The Primer 25K Dock exposes no UART: J7 carries JTAG only, and the
BL616<->FPGA link on B3/C3 reaches no header. That left no way to see why
TangCore stopped during boot, since its status messages go to an overlay
that only exists once the FPGA is programmed.

Bit-bang 9600 8N1 on J7 pin 2 (JTAG TDI / GPIO3), mirroring overlay_status(),
dprint() and printf(). GPIO3 is reassigned to TDI while the MCU programs the
FPGA, so output is buffered across that interval and flushed by
disable_jtag_pins().

debug_uart_task drains the buffer, but it is not created until three lines
before vTaskStartScheduler(). Everything logged during init -- board_init,
SDH, usbh_initialize -- would otherwise never reach the wire, and a hang
anywhere in that sequence would be indistinguishable from a dead UART. So
also transmit synchronously while the scheduler has not started.

Consecutive identical lines collapse to one plus a repeat count, because
main_task re-emits "core_id=-1" about five times a second while no core
answers, and the heartbeat drops to 10 s. Both keep the boot messages
readable on a small serial display.

Three build-time test modes, all off by default:
  DEBUG_UART_SOAK       continuous 0x00 frames; a multimeter reads ~0.3 V
                        against 3.3 V idle, proving the transmit path
  DEBUG_UART_SWEEP      walks the bit period, one letter per candidate
  DEBUG_UART_CALIBRATE  times the bit delay with interrupts on and off

Measured on hardware: the bit period is ~104.6 us (~9560 baud), and
bflb_mtimer_delay_us() behaves identically with interrupts enabled and
disabled. A 3000 mtimer-ms marker takes ~4.6 real seconds, confirming the
40/26 clock ratio DEBUG_UART_BIT_US is derived from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016oqomAUz6WC3hwiRMszouo
